cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Institutional Strain and Substance Coping: Analyzing Perceived Racial Discrimination as a Predictor of Adolescent Marijuana Use"
type: thesis
authors:
  - family-names: Khan
    given-names: Fahad Bin Islam
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0629-9473
abstract: >-
  This cross-sectional study examines perceived racial or ethnic discrimination
  as an institutional strain associated with psychological distress and marijuana
  use among U.S. high school students using the 2023 Youth Risk Behavior Survey.
  The complete-case sample includes 17,268 students. The study reports
  associations rather than causal effects.
year: 2026
institution: University of Mississippi
repository-artifact: https://egrove.olemiss.edu/etd/8839
url: https://khanfahad.com/publications/institutional-strain
keywords:
  - institutional strain
  - General Strain Theory
  - racial discrimination
  - adolescent marijuana use
  - youth substance use
  - Youth Risk Behavior Survey
